  "mirror_step_degrees": 15,
  "scope": "Every property here is measured off the figure, not assigned. Mirror axes are sampled every 15 degrees, so the count is a LOWER BOUND in two ways: an axis lying between samples is missed, and a curve carried as a sampled polyline can fall short of its own ideal. The Sun-in-Circle scores 9 of a possible 12 for exactly that reason, and is left at 9 rather than rounded up to infinite -- widening the tolerance until the expected answer appears is the failure this project exists to prevent. None of this names an orbit: one with no recorded meaning stays UNDETERMINED, and the point of the index is that it can now be asked for rather than filled in.",
  "how_to_query": "python3 tools/ul_cli.py find --closed --components 2; or filter orbits[] on any measured key"
}
